  "name": "Chat with TikTok and Instagram analytics and send weekly Slack briefings using Claude and Postdom",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "3248af1b-40ad-479b-adc3-7e3c1bc0a689",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -720,
        -240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 640,
        "height": 700,
        "content": "## Chat with TikTok and Instagram analytics and send weekly Slack briefings using Claude and Postdom\n\nAsk plain questions like \"Which TikTok did best this week?\" or \"Why did Instagram views drop?\" and a Claude AI agent answers from your real Postdom numbers. Every Monday the same agent writes a short performance briefing and posts it to Slack.\n\nFor marketers, founders and agencies.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Chat Trigger** opens a chat in n8n. **Every Monday** sends the agent a fixed briefing request.\n2. The **Social media analyst** agent runs on Claude with memory and a Think tool, and picks from eight read-only **Postdom** tools: accounts, best posts, account performance, post details, post performance, weekly digest, workspace status and brand brief.\n3. It quotes numbers with their period and says when a platform does not report a metric, instead of showing zero.\n4. Chat questions are answered in the chat. The Monday briefing goes to your Slack channel.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. In [Postdom](https://postdom.com), connect your accounts and create an agent key under **Accounts > Agent keys**. A read-only key is enough.\n2. In n8n, create a **Postdom API** credential and select it on every Postdom tool.\n3. Add an **Anthropic** credential on **Claude chat model**.\n4. Connect Slack and pick a channel in **Post briefing to Slack**.\n5. Open the chat and ask a question, then activate the workflow for Monday briefings.\n\n### Customization tips\n- Edit **Briefing request** to change what the Monday briefing covers.\n- Change the day and time in **Every Monday**.\n- Swap the Chat Trigger for Slack or Telegram.\n\nUses the verified Postdom community node. It runs on n8n Cloud and on self-hosted n8n."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
